      "preview": "הֲרָרִי: adjetivo gentílico: habitante da montanha (?).",
      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">הֲרָרִי</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרָרִי</span></big>  <strong>adjetivo gentílico. (</strong>= <em>habitante da montanha</em> (Thes)? ou derivação de algum nome próprio de lugar desconhecido<strong>)</strong>;—usado somente na identificação de certos heróis de Davi:<br><strong>1.</strong> <strong>a.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁמָּה הַהֲרָרִי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:33\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.33\">2 S 23:33a</a> (cf. Dr) = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:34\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.34\">1 Ch 11:34b</a> (onde se leia provavelmente <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁמָּה</span> em lugar de <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׁגֵה</span>, 𝔊L Σαμαια). <strong>b.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁמָּה בֶּן־אָגֵא הָרָרִי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:11\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.11\">2 S 23:11</a> (leia-se talvez <span dir=\"rtl\">הַהֲרָרִי</span> cf. Dr; mas 𝔊 ὁ Ἁρουχαῖος, 𝔊L ὁ Αραχι, isto é, <span dir=\"rtl\">הָאַרְכִּי</span>? cf. Klo). Acerca de <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁמּוֹת הַהֲרוֹרִי</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:27\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.27\">1 Ch 11:27</a> (𝔊 ὁ Ἁδι, 𝔊L ὁ Αρωρι) ver <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, הֲרוֹרִי\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_הֲרוֹרִי\">הֲרוֹרִי</a> acima, p. 248.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחִיאָם בֶּן־שָׁרָר הָארָרִי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:33\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.33\">2 S 23:33b</a> (leia-se provavelmente <span dir=\"rtl\">הַהֲרָרִי</span>) = <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲחִיאָם בֶּן־שָׂכָר הַהֲרָרִי</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:35\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.35\">1 Ch 11:35</a>.",
